---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import recordedReceipt from '../../../research/recovery/results/latest.json';

type Violation = { code: string; detail: string };
type Event = Record<string, unknown>;
type Run = { id: string; control?: string | boolean | null; grade: { passed: boolean; violations: Violation[] }; trace: { events: Event[]; queue: unknown[]; reports: unknown[]; observations?: unknown[]; worker_runs?: unknown[]; framework_calls?: number } };
type Receipt = { generatedAt: string; environment: { python: string; sqlite: string; platform: string; frameworks: Record<string, string> }; summary: { validPassed: number; validTotal: number; controlsFailed: number; controlsTotal: number; negativeRejected: number; negativeTotal: number }; runs: Run[]; negativeCases: { id: string; expectedCode: string; detected: boolean; violations: Violation[] }[]; manifest: Record<string, unknown> };
const receipt = recordedReceipt as Receipt;
const source = 'https://github.com/valorifutures/softcat.ai/tree/main/research/recovery';
const labels: Record<string, string> = { clean: 'Clean completion', delayed_revocation: 'Delayed revocation notification', lost_ack_restart: 'Lost reply, worker restart', restart_before_commit_revoke: 'Restart, then revoke before commit', identical_retry: 'Identical request retried', conflicting_retry: 'Same key, changed payload', allow_revoked: 'Permit a revoked write', forget_idempotency: 'Disable duplicate protection', false_success: 'Claim success without a reply' };
const name = (value: string) => labels[value] || value.replaceAll('-', ' ').replaceAll('_', ' ');
const validRuns = receipt.runs.filter(run => run.control === 'enforced');
const controls = receipt.runs.filter(run => run.control !== 'enforced');
const lostReply = validRuns.find(run => /lost|ack/.test(run.id));
const recordedAt = new Date(receipt.generatedAt).toLocaleString('en-GB', { day: 'numeric', month: 'long', year: 'numeric', hour: '2-digit', minute: '2-digit', timeZone: 'UTC' });
const serialise = (value: unknown) => JSON.stringify(value, null, 2);
const eventTitle = (event: Event) => name(String(event.type || event.kind || 'recorded event'));
const commands = [
  'python3.12 -m venv .venv-recovery',
  '.venv-recovery/bin/python -m pip install --require-hashes --only-binary=:all: -r research/recovery/requirements.lock',
  ".venv-recovery/bin/python -m unittest discover -s research/recovery -p 'test_*.py'",
  '.venv-recovery/bin/python research/recovery/run.py --verify research/recovery/results/latest.json',
].join('\n');
---

<BaseLayout title="Research: recovery without invented success" description="A lost reply is not a failed action. Inspect SOFT CAT's deterministic LangGraph and PydanticAI recovery experiment, recorded failures and runnable open source." breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Research', url: '/research/' }, { name: 'Recovery', url: '/research/recovery/' }]}>
  <div class="workshop-shell recovery-page">
    <a class="back-link" href="/research/">← The first authority experiment</a>
    <header class="recovery-hero">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">OPEN RESEARCH / RECOVERY STUDY</p>
        <h1>A lost reply<br />is not a<br /><em>failed action.</em></h1>
        <p class="lead">Before an agent tries again, it needs to know what already happened.</p>
        <p>We put two real framework runtimes through controlled disruption. Their decisions are scripted. The test is whether recovery preserves permission, avoids duplicate effects and reports uncertainty honestly.</p>
        <div class="hero-actions"><a href="#lost-reply" class="workshop-button primary">Follow the missing reply <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><a href={source} class="text-link">Inspect the source <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
      </div>
      <aside class="execution-card" aria-labelledby="execution-heading">
        <p class="receipt-label">RECORDED LOCAL EXECUTION</p>
        <h2 id="execution-heading">Real frameworks.<br />Fixed decisions.</h2>
        <p>LangGraph <strong>{receipt.environment.frameworks.langgraph}</strong><br />PydanticAI slim <strong>{receipt.environment.frameworks['pydantic-ai-slim']}</strong></p>
        <dl class="execution-counts">
          <div><dt>Valid development cases accepted</dt><dd>{receipt.summary.validPassed}<span> / {receipt.summary.validTotal}</span></dd></div>
          <div><dt>Deficient controls rejected</dt><dd>{receipt.summary.controlsFailed}<span> / {receipt.summary.controlsTotal}</span></dd></div>
          <div><dt>Corrupted outcomes rejected</dt><dd>{receipt.summary.negativeRejected}<span> / {receipt.summary.negativeTotal}</span></dd></div>
        </dl>
        <p class="recorded-date">Recorded <time datetime={receipt.generatedAt}>{recordedAt} UTC</time></p>
        <p class="execution-limit">No remote model calls. No live customer systems. No claim of agent intelligence or a completed agent benchmark.</p>
      </aside>
    </header>

    <nav class="section-links" aria-label="Recovery study sections"><a href="#lost-reply">The missing reply</a><a href="#cases">Recorded cases</a><a href="#challenge">Challenge the checker</a><a href="#reproduce">Source and reproduction</a><a href="#boundary">The boundary</a></nav>

    <section id="lost-reply" class="study-section" aria-labelledby="lost-heading">
      <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">01 / THE UNCERTAINTY WINDOW</p><h2 id="lost-heading">The write survives.<br />The reply does not.</h2><p>A worker can disappear after a queue commit. Calling that a failure and sending a fresh request risks doing the work twice.</p><p>In this case, a local worker process exits. A replacement consults the durable record before reporting the outcome.</p></div>
      <div class="section-content">
        <ol class="recovery-sequence" aria-label="The recovery contract">
          <li><span class="step-label">COMMIT</span><h3>One durable effect.</h3><p>The local queue records the request before the reply reaches its caller.</p></li>
          <li class="uncertain"><span class="step-label">UNCERTAIN</span><h3>No reply is no answer.</h3><p>The caller cannot infer success or failure from the missing acknowledgement.</p></li>
          <li><span class="step-label">RECONCILE</span><h3>Ask the authority.</h3><p>The replacement worker uses a separate read grant to check the original request against the durable state.</p></li>
        </ol>
        <p class="caption">The contract above describes the case. The recorded execution below is the evidence. This page does not run agents or simulate live activity.</p>
        {lostReply && <details class="featured-trace"><summary><span><strong>Inspect the lost-reply execution</strong><small>{lostReply.trace.events.length} recorded events · grader {lostReply.grade.passed ? 'accepted' : 'rejected'}</small></span></summary><p class="caption">Sequence is local event order. It is not distributed propagation latency.</p><ol class="event-list">{lostReply.trace.events.map((event, index) => <li><span class="event-number" aria-hidden="true">{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span><details><summary>{eventTitle(event)}</summary><pre tabindex="0" aria-label={`Recorded event ${index + 1}`}><code>{serialise(event)}</code></pre></details></li>)}</ol><details class="final-record"><summary>Compare queue, reports and worker records</summary><pre tabindex="0" aria-label="Lost-reply final record"><code>{serialise({ grade: lostReply.grade, queue: lostReply.trace.queue, reports: lostReply.trace.reports, observations: lostReply.trace.observations, worker_runs: lostReply.trace.worker_runs, framework_calls: lostReply.trace.framework_calls })}</code></pre></details></details>}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="cases" class="study-section" aria-labelledby="cases-heading">
      <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">02 / RECORDED CASES</p><h2 id="cases-heading">Make disruption<br />part of the test.</h2><p>Normal completion, delayed notification, process restart, retry and a changed payload exercise different failure paths.</p><p>A separate grader checks each event record, queue and outcome report.</p><a class="text-link" href="/research/recovery/receipt.json">Open the full JSON receipt <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
      <div class="section-content"><div class="case-grid">{validRuns.map(run => <article class="case-card"><p class="case-name">{name(run.id)}</p><h3 class:list={[{ rejected: !run.grade.passed }]}>{run.grade.passed ? 'Accepted' : 'Rejected'}</h3><p>{run.trace.queue.length} queue {run.trace.queue.length === 1 ? 'effect' : 'effects'} · {run.trace.events.length} recorded events</p><details><summary>Inspect the actual record</summary><pre tabindex="0" aria-label={`${name(run.id)} execution record`}><code>{serialise({ grade: run.grade, ...run.trace })}</code></pre></details></article>)}</div><div class="contract-note"><h3>Revoked does not mean undone.</h3><p>Revocation blocks a new effect at the local commit boundary. It cannot reverse an earlier committed effect. A delayed notification must not create extra permission.</p><p>A repeated request needs the same job, request key and payload. Reusing the key with changed content must surface a conflict.</p></div></div>
    </section>

    <section id="challenge" class="study-section" aria-labelledby="challenge-heading">
      <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">03 / CHALLENGE THE CHECKER</p><h2 id="challenge-heading">A reassuring report<br />is not enough.</h2><p>Deliberately deficient controls and corrupted records test whether the grader catches the wrong outcome.</p><p>These are seeded faults. They are not discovered vulnerabilities or zero-days.</p></div>
      <div class="section-content"><h3 class="group-heading">Deficient controls</h3><div class="disclosure-list">{controls.map(run => <details><summary><span>{name(run.id)}</span><strong class:list={[{ rejected: run.grade.passed }]}>{run.grade.passed ? 'Unexpectedly accepted' : 'Rejected'}</strong></summary><ul class="violations">{run.grade.violations.map(violation => <li><code>{violation.code}</code><p>{violation.detail}</p></li>)}</ul><details><summary>Inspect the control trace</summary><pre tabindex="0" aria-label={`${name(run.id)} control trace`}><code>{serialise(run.trace)}</code></pre></details></details>)}</div><h3 class="group-heading negative-heading">Corrupted outcome checks</h3><div class="disclosure-list">{receipt.negativeCases.map(test => <details><summary><span>{name(test.id)}</span><strong class:list={[{ rejected: !test.detected }]}>{test.detected ? 'Detected' : 'Missed'}</strong></summary><p class="expected-code">Expected rejection: <code>{test.expectedCode}</code></p><ul class="violations">{test.violations.map(violation => <li><code>{violation.code}</code><p>{violation.detail}</p></li>)}</ul></details>)}</div><p class="caption">A separate grader implementation and agent review are useful checks. They do not establish independent reproduction or an exhaustive adversarial assessment.</p></div>
    </section>

    <section id="reproduce" class="study-section" aria-labelledby="reproduce-heading">
      <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">04 / SOURCE AND REPRODUCTION</p><h2 id="reproduce-heading">Bring the failing case<br />with the claim.</h2><p>Inspect the code, pinned dependencies, fixture and receipt together. The recorded traces and grading results are embedded in this page, so inspecting them does not depend on a download working.</p><a class="text-link" href={source}>Open source and run instructions <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
      <div class="section-content"><p class="reproduction-copy">The research runner uses LangGraph and PydanticAI with a deterministic <code>FunctionModel</code>. Framework execution is real. Responses are fixed by code, so these results do not measure reasoning or generalisation. Dependency installation needs package access. The experiment itself needs no provider key.</p><p class="reproduction-copy">From a repository checkout, using Python 3.12 on Linux x64:</p><pre tabindex="0" aria-label="Commands to install and verify the recovery harness"><code>{commands}</code></pre><p class="caption">Verification reruns the deterministic cases and compares the recorded evidence. For a fresh receipt, run <code>.venv-recovery/bin/python research/recovery/run.py</code>. This writes JSON to standard output.</p><dl class="environment"><div><dt>Recorded Python</dt><dd>{receipt.environment.python}</dd></div><div><dt>SQLite</dt><dd>{receipt.environment.sqlite}</dd></div><div><dt>Platform</dt><dd>{receipt.environment.platform}</dd></div><div><dt>Our research code</dt><dd><a href="https://github.com/valorifutures/softcat.ai/blob/main/research/LICENSE">Apache-2.0</a></dd></div></dl><p class="caption">Framework dependencies retain their own licences. No monetary execution cost is measured. No model calls does not mean no computing cost.</p><details class="manifest"><summary>Inspect the execution manifest</summary><pre tabindex="0" aria-label="Recovery execution manifest"><code>{serialise(receipt.manifest)}</code></pre></details></div>
    </section>

    <section id="boundary" class="study-section" aria-labelledby="boundary-heading">
      <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">05 / THE BOUNDARY</p><h2 id="boundary-heading">Local evidence.<br />Bounded conclusions.</h2></div>
      <div class="section-content"><ul class="limits"><li><strong>One authoritative SQLite store.</strong> Revocation and commits share a local ordering boundary. This does not establish distributed consensus, partition tolerance or cross-organisation security.</li><li><strong>A trusted harness.</strong> The SQLite host, registry, harness-supplied caller identity, worker and grader are trusted. Grant IDs are local handles, not authentication. Workers can access the database, so this does not contain a malicious worker or compromised host.</li><li><strong>A custom local hand-off.</strong> Frameworks exchange local JSON. This is not A2A or MCP wire interoperability.</li><li><strong>Known development cases.</strong> These are constructed cases, not a held-out benchmark. Their denominators do not estimate performance on unseen work.</li><li><strong>Framework integration before model evaluation.</strong> Scripted responses do not establish useful cooperation, a swarm advantage or completion of the full agent-execution gate.</li><li><strong>A local simulated queue.</strong> The effect is a remediation request in a test database. No repair runs on a real network, customer system or external service.</li></ul><div class="next-step"><p class="eyebrow">WHAT WOULD CHANGE THE EVIDENCE?</p><h3>Fresh model decisions. Fair comparisons.</h3><p>First, separate authenticated caller identity and the action boundary from the worker. A subsequent model evaluation needs a single-agent baseline, configured access and spending limits, calibrated budgets and a frozen disjoint test set. All scheduled failures and timeouts must remain visible.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/valorifutures/softcat.ai/blob/main/docs/research-programme.md">Read the wider programme <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><p class="charter">Our <a href="/constitution/">constitution</a> keeps the distinction between a working artefact, a measured finding and an independent reproduction.</p></div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .recovery-page { padding-block: 2rem 5rem; }
  .back-link { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; min-height: 44px; color: #a6b09e; font-size: .72rem; margin-bottom: 2rem; }
